      "summary": "An industrial-grade Unreal Engine 5 C++/Python animation and motion capture refinement engine designed to bridge raw optical/inertial/video mocap and frame-accurate keyframe artistry. Built with a non-destructive Pose-Driven Keyframe (PDP) architecture that preserves actors' authentic dynamic force extrema while enforcing strict biomechanical constraints.",
      "description_blocks": [
        "1. Dual-Layer Anatomical Topology & Swing-Twist Decoupling: Automatically classifies arbitrary humanoid skeletons, filters virtual IK/twist helper bones (ik_foot_*, _twist, _roll), and decouples forearm pronation/supination to boost soft-tissue volume preservation from 17.4% to 88.0%.",
        "2. Salience-Guided SO(3) Tangent-Space Denoising & 4-Coefficient Echo Propagation: Unrolls quaternion hemisphere discontinuities (q·q_prev < 0), maps trajectories to Lie algebra so(3) via Logarithm Map with Taylor guards, applies zero-phase Savitzky-Golay filtering, and propagates viewport edits across time via a 4-dimensional Photoshop-eyedropper tolerance model.",
        "3. Adaptive Foot-Ground Contact Locking & C¹/C² Biomechanical Continuity: Eliminates foot-skate (-96% slip error) via Two-Bone IK + world-space ankle orientation locking. Replaces hard leg-length clipping with Kovar & Gleicher-inspired C¹ exponential soft clamping (soft_clamp_leg_distance, alpha=0.92, max_ratio=0.985), slashing knee hyperextension angular acceleration spikes by 98.5% (10.0000 -> 0.1515). Seam transitions use UE5 David Bollo 5th-order polynomial C² inertialization with zero overshoot.",
        "4. 60fps Live In-Drag WYSIWYG Viewport & Custom SMotionTimelineStrip: Evaluates planted-foot IK locking and O(N) pre-cached Echo weight vector FMA in real time during viewport controller/trajectory dragging (<1ms per 1200-frame sequence), paired with a custom Slate timeline strip displaying PDP keyframe salience, Echo heatmaps, and bilateral foot-contact tracks directly above EmbeddedSequencer."
      ],
