      "path": "/vr-body-mapping-padagogy-practive",
      "url": "https://breakfast012.com/vr-body-mapping-padagogy-practive",
      "title": "Jiayi Wu - VR Body Mapping - Pedagogy Practice",
      "image_count": 1,
      "embed_count": 1,
      "full_text": "Jiayi Wu - VR Body Mapping - Pedagogy Practice Changemaker Evaluation & Impact Project (UAL, 2024–2025)Principal Investigator: Kevin J. BrazantCo-researcher & VR Lead: Jiayi WuCo-researcher: Chiara Portinari, Saranya SatheeshFunded by: UAL Climate, Racial and Social Justice FundProject OverviewThis project evaluates and documents UAL Changemakers, a student–staff partnership programme that co-creates inclusive pedagogies and embeds equity and social justice in curriculum design.As the co-researcher and technical lead, I developed the VR body-mapping prototype that extends traditional reflective evaluation into an embodied, multisensory form. Participants used immersive tools to visualise and externalise emotional experiences related to identity, belonging, and justice.A preview of the prototype was presented in the project’s pre-video, demonstrating how embodied gestures and spatial drawing can reveal affective dimensions of learning that are difficult to capture through conventional surveys or interviews. RecognitionTom Burns Memorial Award 2025 – ALDinHE (UK)People’s Prize for Equality and Diversity 2025 – UAL Knowledge Exchange Staff Awards ↑Back to Top Powered by Adobe Portfolio",
